 "level_notes": {
  "1": "The Arm Architecture Reference Manuals are the normative definition (free with registration-free download, but rendered by JavaScript on developer.arm.com, so no deep links); the Arm ABI (AAPCS) lives in ARM-software/abi-aa. Arm also publishes the architecture in its machine-readable ASL, from which sail-arm is generated.",
  "0": "No single reference implementation: GNU as, LLVM's integrated assembler and armasm are the assemblers; QEMU and Unicorn emulate the ISA."
 },
